content.text:
I deleted 181 demo accounts from production: the 12 broken ones and 169 unclaimed demo guests older than 7 days.

- **Backup:** a full backup of the production database, plus the list of deleted IDs, is in `/root/demo-cleanup-backup-1793066901` on the VPS.
- **What was removed:** each account and all its rows in every table, in one go. None had support messages, alliance memberships or map pieces, and none had been active in the last week.
- **Checks:**
  - none of the deleted IDs remain;
  - no orphaned finance or resort rows are left;
  - the 294 normal accounts are untouched;
  - the home, login and leaderboard pages respond.
- **Kept:** the 25 demos started in the last 7 days, plus one more explained below.

One account I deliberately didn't delete: #338 ("Demo Director 3860", created 10 October). It has a real person's email address on it, so it looks like someone tried to save their demo as a permanent account. It's still marked as a demo and wasn't used after that day, so they may not be able to log in to it.

